The MinLZ HLS encoder and parallel CRC32C implementation are new MIT-licensed
code. They implement the public MinLZ specification v1.0 and do not copy the
official CPU encoder. The host decoder is the external github.com/minio/minlz
module under its own Apache-2.0 license; that dependency is not relicensed.
Specification: https://github.com/minio/minlz/blob/v1.2.3/SPEC.md

zstd-literal-buffer.patch, zstd-frame-fse.patch, zstd-fifo.patch and
zstd-huffman-padding.patch modify Apache-2.0 upstream
headers in a private build directory. The original library checkout remains
unchanged. The upstream license is included as LICENSE.Vitis-Libraries.
